  <front>
    <title abbrev="Mail Action Protocol">Mail Action Protocol (MAP)</title>
    <seriesInfo name="Internet-Draft" value="draft-mailschema-mail-action-protocol-00"/>
    <author fullname="Kam Low" initials="K." surname="Low">
      <organization>MailSchema</organization>
      <address><email>oss@0state.com</email><uri>https://mailschema.org/</uri></address>
    </author>
    <date year="2026" month="October" day="2"/>
    <area>Applications and Real-Time</area>
    <workgroup>Individual Submission</workgroup>
    <keyword>email</keyword><keyword>agents</keyword><keyword>structured email</keyword>
    <abstract>
      <t>The Mail Action Protocol (MAP) describes a service proposal in email
      so a recipient or an agent acting for that recipient can evaluate it
      and use the service's existing operations. Versioned contracts define
      the proposal's data, operations, and effects. A trusted service
      implementation resolves those operations independently of the email;
      authoritative readback and an atomic terms-version check bind a
      credentialed decision to the current proposal. MAP uses Structured
      Email's JSON-LD and MIME representation. It defines no general action
      endpoint, execution envelope, identity provider, or permission language.
      This document specifies Core 0.3, an HTTP binding, and an optional
      experimental bearer-capability binding limited to refusal, protective
      reports, and confirmation of an initiated address-validation request.</t>
    </abstract>
  </front>
  <middle>
    <!-- Generated from specifications/map-0.3. Edit its sources, not this projection. -->
    <!-- specification -->
    <section anchor="implementation-status"><name>Implementation Status</name>
      <t>This section follows <xref target="RFC7942"/> and is to be removed
      before publication as an RFC. The specification source, four Draft
      Registry contracts, schemas, examples, and conformance scenarios are at
      <eref target="https://github.com/mailschema/mailschema/tree/docs/map-0-3-specification/specifications/map-0.3"/>.
      Artifact checks establish shape, digest consistency, and offline
      JSON-LD interpretation. Runtime scenarios are unimplemented skeletons.
      No MAP 0.3 runtime conformance or independent interoperability is claimed.
      Existing MAP 0.2 implementations do not establish MAP 0.3 conformance.</t>
      <t>Feedback is sought on receiver authentication evidence, existing API
      readback mappings, atomic version enforcement, and the limited
      capability binding. The latter requires explicit opt-in and remains
      experimental pending implementation evidence. No MCP binding is
      specified here. This document is prepared as an individual submission;
      it does not assert adoption by the Structured Email working group.</t>
    </section>
  </middle>
